<https://w3id.org/aiprov/prov/claim/c-human-steps-fix> a aiprov:Claim ;
    rdfs:label "provlog claim and source now refuse human-confirmed, human-read and lit-read unless the agent is a registered HumanAgent, as promote does. Six new tests in tests/test_human_steps.py cover refusal, acceptance by a registered human, an unchanged graph file after a refusal and the ai-confirmed control. The suite passed with 30 tests on CPython 3.13 (uv run --extra dev pytest -q); CI on 3.10 and 3.12 was not run locally."@en ;
    prov:wasAttributedTo agent:claude-sonnet-5-5 ;
    prov:wasGeneratedBy <https://w3id.org/aiprov/prov/activity/fix-human-only-steps> ;
    aiprov:verificationState verif:unverified .

<https://w3id.org/aiprov/prov/claim/c-human-steps-scope> a aiprov:Claim ;
    rdfs:label "Not changed by the fix: claim still accepts states outside the ladder (adopters record contested), validate still only warns for a graph edited by hand, and nothing checks an AuditPass written outside provlog."@en ;
    prov:wasAttributedTo agent:claude-sonnet-5-5 ;
    prov:wasGeneratedBy <https://w3id.org/aiprov/prov/activity/fix-human-only-steps> ;
    aiprov:verificationState verif:unverified .

<https://w3id.org/aiprov/prov/claim/c-logging-instant-is-not-a-span> a aiprov:Claim ;
    rdfs:label "provlog recorded the moment a log line was appended in the field a reader takes for the duration of the work, and the consequence is misattribution rather than untidiness. Measured in a consuming repository on 2026-10-26: fourteen activities of one agent session carried prov:endedAtTime minus prov:startedAtTime of 0.35 to 1.27 seconds, for work whose real spans, derived from the first and last turn timestamps of the same session's harness record, were 916.6 and 444.4 seconds for two of the runs. The cause is that cmd_log wrote prov:endedAtTime as the current time unconditionally while --started was optional and seldom passed, so an activity logged in arrears is indistinguishable from one that genuinely took a second. This matters because the model in force can change inside a session through a reroute, a fallback or a manual switch, which was observed twice in one evening on the same session: attribution then follows the instant of logging rather than the window of work, and a perfectly valid graph can name the wrong model. The change is additive: aiprov:recordedAtTime is always written and states when the record was made, log --ended takes the end of the work and still defaults to now, and validate reports a session activity whose span is under a second or absent as a warning rather than a failure, because a genuinely short activity is possible and aiprov cannot distinguish the two. Records written before the change remain distinguishable by the absence of recordedAtTime. Thirty-four tests pass, two of them new and covering both directions. Not established: whether a sub-second threshold is the right boundary, and aiprov still has no way to obtain a true end time itself; it can only stop overwriting the field that would hold one."@en ;
    prov:wasAttributedTo agent:claude-opus-alias ;
    prov:wasGeneratedBy <https://w3id.org/aiprov/prov/activity/work-span-vs-record-time> ;
    aiprov:verificationState verif:unverified .

<https://w3id.org/aiprov/prov/claim/c-logo-provenance> a aiprov:Claim ;
    rdfs:label "The three badge files are byte-identical to the output of assets/make_icon.py run on the source picture (sha256 checked twice); the source is the inline image the owner pasted into the session, 1024 x 1024 px, sha256 670dc0f0. Model setting and prompt use are the owner's statements."@en ;
    prov:wasAttributedTo agent:claude-opus-5-5 ;
    prov:wasGeneratedBy <https://w3id.org/aiprov/prov/activity/logo-salmon-badge> ;
    aiprov:verificationState verif:ai-confirmed .

